[ANALYSIS — root cause of D7 FAIL, confirmed by RTL reading]
Symptom: ERROR_STATUS=0x200 (bit9 E_BIT_PROTOCOL) latched after a fully
legitimate RESULT_ACK; everything else exact (tail advanced, ownership
cleared, all T4 golden values hit). STATUS bit3 ERROR set accordingly.
Cause: same-edge race in yolo_reg_file.sv A_RESULT_ACK path —
  * ack_consume_pulse asserts at edge E1 (registered pulse)
  * ring_tail_ptr_o ALSO increments at E1 (same always block, lines ~275-278)
  * yolo_result_ring.sv:173 samples not_empty_o during the pulse cycle C1;
    not_empty_o = (head != tail) with tail ALREADY advanced -> head==tail
    when ACK drains the last entry -> false "ack on empty ring" latched.
Fires on every legitimate ACK that empties the ring (the common
single-frame case). With IRQ armed, every frame would raise a false
error interrupt; real protocol errors become indistinguishable.
Why 81/81 sim missed it: TB never asserts full ERROR_STATUS==0 after ACK
(T5 checks are masked single-bit, tb lines 429-443). Coverage hole.
Datapath impact: none observed (tail/ownership/ring window all correct).
Proposed fix (3-line, one file): move the tail increment out of the
A_RESULT_ACK write decode into a `if (ack_consume_pulse || ack_drop_pulse)
ring_tail_ptr_o <= ring_tail_ptr_o + 1;` one cycle later, so the ring
samples the pulse against the pre-increment tail. Add TB full-value
assertion ERROR_STATUS==0 after T4's ACK.
